7. Use HTTPS: Always use HTTPS to encrypt data in transit, including passwords. This helps protect passwords from being intercepted by attackers during transmission.

By following these best practices, you can ensure that user passwords are securely hashed and stored in your database, reducing the risk of unauthorized access and data breaches.
